 explain hypercalcemia and constitutional symptoms"], "alarm_features": ["Constitutional weight loss", "Hypercalcemia (Ca2+ > 12 mg/dL)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Hyperparathyroidism with Hypercalcemia", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.036, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The finding weakly contradicts primary hyperparathyroidism (B1) but remains neutral for other hypercalcemia mechanisms."]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Malignancy with Hypercalcemia", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.6001746440060433, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["The subacute presentation with constitutional symptoms and hypercalcemia is consistent with paraneoplastic syndromes (moderate_for B2), though the absence of t…"], "evidence_against": ["The absence of tumor markers weakly argues against malignancy (B2) but does not exclude it."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B2.1", "B2.2", "B2.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 3.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_relevance": 0.8, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["humoral hypercalcemia of malignancy", "multiple myeloma", "squamous cell carcinoma", "primary hyperparathyroidism"]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Vitamin D Toxicity / Excess", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.03, "danger": 0.5, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The absence of hypophosphatemia and 25-OH vitamin D elevation strongly contradicts vitamin D toxicity (B3)."]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Reactive Hypercalcemia / Non-malignant Granulomatous Disorders", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.09268292682926828, "posterior": 0.14165472836015058, "danger": 0.4, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expan